  "notes": "{立|た}ち{退|の}く is used for formally leaving a property or area.\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- {立|た}ち{退|の}きを{命|めい}じられる: to be ordered to vacate\n- {立|た}ち{退|の}き{料|りょう}: eviction compensation\n- {立|た}ち{退|の}き{要求|ようきゅう}: demand to vacate\n- {強制|きょうせい}{立|た}ち{退|の}き: forced eviction\n\nUSAGE NOTES:\n- {立|た}ち{退|の}かせる (causative): to evict, to force out\n- {立|た}ち{退|の}かされる (passive): to be evicted\n\nRELATED WORDS:\n- {退去|たいきょ}する: to leave, to vacate (more formal)\n- {明|あ}け{渡|わた}す: to hand over, to vacate",
